> monster spoilers[*] for a list of those monsters that give you
> poison resistance without being poisonous to you. Some poisonous
> monsters confer the resistance as well, but the drawbacks (lost
> strength, or even death) are usually not worth to risk that, at
> least as long as you haven't found some means to immediately
> restore your lost stats.
> 
> [*] Any list I could give you off the top of my head would be
> incomplete. 

Then let Wikihack give the list: 
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Poison_resistance -- it even tells you 
what dangers there are of eating a particular corpse. A good bet if 
you get an early wish (and have nothing better to wish for) is a 
blessed tin of green dragon meat (tinning makes poisonous and acidic 
corpses safe to eat, provided there's nothing else dangerous about 
the corpse).

Alternatively, you can try eating one of the poisonous corpses on the 
list if you have extrinsic PR or can handle 1d15 damage and 1d4 STR 
loss (poisonous corpses never cause instadeath, though the HP loss 
can still kill you).


